// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6130 new: Node.js Package Manager Supply-Chain Execution Hunts (Windows/Linux/macOS)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6130
// Pull request author: NikoCosmico01
// Change: new rule
// Title: Node.js Package Manager Spawning Download Or Reverse Shell - macOS
// Sigma ID: c210982b-6001-4f1f-96ad-70fef301e066
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Nicolò Thei, NikoCosmico01
// Date: 2026-07-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.004, T1059.006, T1059.007, initial-access, T1195.002
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects a Node.js runtime or JavaScript package manager (node / bun, the executors behind npm,
//   pnpm and yarn) spawning a shell that downloads-and-executes payloads or opens a reverse shell,
//   or invoking a scripting interpreter with a network download cradle. This behaviour is
//   characteristic of install-time "lifecycle hook" (preinstall/postinstall) abuse used in modern
//   npm supply-chain compromises (e.g. Shai-Hulud, the @tanstack "Mini Shai-Hulud" and the axios
//   "plain-crypto-js" campaigns), which also target macOS developer workstations. Unlike campaign-
//   specific indicator rules, this is a generic behavioural hunt intended to surface the next
//   compromise before its IOCs are published.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate "preinstall"/"postinstall" scripts that fetch prebuilt native binaries via curl/wget. Baseline per project and allowlist known-good packages.
//   - Build tooling that invokes Python/Perl/Ruby for setup tasks.
// References:
//   - https://socket.dev/blog/tanstack-npm-packages-compromised-mini-shai-hulud-supply-chain-attack
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/supply-chain-compromise-axios-npm-package
//   - https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/using-npm/scripts
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c32049570c6068e047800b4f7d973350b6a4360c/rules-threat-hunting/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_nodejs_pkg_manager_susp_child.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/node" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/bun") and (FolderPath endswith "/bash" or FolderPath endswith "/dash" or FolderPath endswith "/ksh" or FolderPath endswith "/sh" or FolderPath endswith "/zsh") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "base64 -D" or ProcessCommandLine contains "chmod +x" or ProcessCommandLine contains "curl " or ProcessCommandLine contains "/dev/tcp/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "nohup " or ProcessCommandLine contains "| bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "| sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "osascript" or ProcessCommandLine contains "wget ")) or ((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/node" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/bun") and (FolderPath endswith "/perl" or FolderPath endswith "/php" or FolderPath endswith "/python" or FolderPath endswith "/python3" or FolderPath endswith "/ruby") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "b64decode" or ProcessCommandLine contains "base64" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/dev/tcp/" or ProcessCommandLine contains "socket" or ProcessCommandLine contains "urllib"))
